&lt;p class="eyebrow"&gt;A LITTLE ABOUT ME&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Hi, I'm Arailym.&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
  I'm a Master's student in Applied Business Analytics at Boston
  University with a background in project management and a growing
  focus on data-driven decision-making.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
  I enjoy connecting analytical methods with real business questions,
  turning complex information into clear insights and practical
  recommendations.
&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;img src="images/about-me.jpg" alt="Arailym in a professional setting"&gt;




01 — BACKGROUND


Professional Background

Before my master’s, I worked in project management, coordinating teams, managing documentation, and supporting process improvements. These experiences shaped my interest in how data and strategy come together to create meaningful business outcomes.

&lt;div&gt;
  &lt;h3&gt;Experience&lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Project management and team coordination&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
  &lt;h3&gt;Education&lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;M.S. in Applied Business Analytics, Boston University&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
  &lt;h3&gt;Focus&lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Data analysis and informed decision-making&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;




02 — MY APPROACH


How I Approach Problems

I enjoy breaking down complex problems, identifying patterns in data, and turning findings into clear, actionable recommendations. I value structured thinking, attention to detail, and effective communication because good analysis is not just about the numbers, but about the decisions they help inform.

&lt;span&gt;Problem solving&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span&gt;Data analysis&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span&gt;Visualization&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span&gt;Business strategy&lt;/span&gt;




&lt;p class="eyebrow"&gt;03 — BEYOND THE NUMBERS&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Beyond the Numbers&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
  Outside of analytics, I'm drawn to travel, cities, and culture.
  Exploring new places gives me fresh perspectives and deepens my
  curiosity about people, behavior, and how businesses adapt to
  different environments.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
  I also appreciate the little things: a new café, interesting
  architecture, and the everyday moments that make a place memorable.
&lt;/p&gt;

